WLS DECODER ON REAL CIRCUITS  (v72 rerun, decoder is the only change)
========================================================================================================
  R = 0.45, 4 repeats. Identical circuits and shots for both
  decoders; only the reduction of the shot record differs.

    N   M   T total  1-cos marg  1-cos wls  1-cos SPSA  wls/marg  SPSA/wls  SPSA/marg
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4  24     32768     0.08735    0.08553     0.23834      0.98      2.79       2.73
    4  24    131072     0.01955    0.01915     0.23104      0.98     12.06      11.82
  ...................................................................................
    6  36     32768     0.11977    0.11839     0.29578      0.99      2.50       2.47
    6  36    131072     0.03837    0.03765     0.25621      0.98      6.81       6.68
  ...................................................................................

  'wls/marg' below 1 means the decoder helps; the last two columns are the
  QLTO/SPSA ratio under each decoder, against v72's 5.66x (N=4) and 5.21x
  (N=6) which were measured with the marginal decoder.

  A win here is free: the circuits, the shots and the counts are identical,
  and only the arithmetic applied to them changes. A loss would mean the
  real landscape has higher-order Walsh content that a main-effects-only
  regression is misspecified against, which the synthetic test could not see.
